[ti:Week04-Mon.mp3]

[00:00.00]concrete 熟义 n. 混凝土‖a. 混凝土制的；具体的；有形的‖v. 用混凝土覆盖 示例 ① But such concrete hazards are beside the point. It's the dangers parents can't—and may never—quantify that occur all of a sudden. 但是这些具体的危险不是重点，重点是那些父母无法——也许永远也不能——进行量化的突然发生的危险。（2009. 12）② It's more difficult to think in abstract terms rather than in the concrete. 抽象思考要比结合具体事物来思考难一些。
[00:08.34]notion 熟义 n. 观念，信念，理念 示例 ① Where do girls get the notion that they need to be thin in order to be considered beautiful? 女孩们是从哪里得到 “瘦即是美”这一观念的？（2009. 6） ② I accept the notion that greed is not a good thing. 我接受贪婪不是什么好事的观念。
[00:13.56]beam 熟义 n. 光线‖v. 放出束状的光（或热） 示例 ① A smartphone strapped to the device beams back video. 设备上绑有一个智能手机，会将视频传送回去。（The Economist）② He beamed at the audiences. 他笑容满面地面对观众。
[00:17.60]commence 熟义 v. 开始发生；开始，着手 示例 ① Developing economies such as Mexico and Brazil would commence reductions around 2040-2045. 发展中国家，例如墨西哥和巴西，将会在2040至2045 年左右开始减排。（The Guardian）② The event commenced with a welcome speech by the principal. 这次活动以校长致欢迎词开场。
[00:23.82]gap 熟义 n. 裂口，缝隙；分歧，差距 示例 ① The most selective private schools —Harvard, Yale, and Princeton—show almost no gap between black and white graduation rates. 在录取条件最严格的私立大学——哈佛、耶鲁和普林斯顿——黑人学生和白人学生的毕业率几乎没有差距。（2011. 6）② The gap between the rich and the poor is widening. 贫富之间的差距正在拉大。
[00:30.65]span 熟义 n. 持续时间；跨度；范围‖v. 持续，贯穿；涵盖，包括 示例 ① If that project takes off, it could become the world's largest water-quality trading programme, spanning as many as eight states and allowing trading between 46 power plants, thousands of wastewater facilities and about 230,000 farmers. 这项计划一旦启动，就将成为世界上最大的水质量贸易计划，其范围涵盖八个州，可以实现 46家发电厂、数千个废水处理站和23万农民之间的贸易。（The Economist）② I worked with her over a span of ten years. 我和她共事达十年之久。 语料 Life is but a span. 人生苦短。
[00:41.71]psychological 熟义 a. 心理的，精神上的；心理学的，关于心理学的 示例 ① It all depends on developmental issue, maturity, and the psychological and emotional makeup of that child. 这完全取决于那个孩子的成长状况、成熟程度以及他们的心理及情感状况。（2009. 6）② The defeat in the last game gave them a psychological disadvantage. 上场比赛的失败让他们在心理上处于劣势。
[00:48.85]diminish 熟义 v. 减少，缩减，降低 示例 ① These changes have also led to habitat loss and to diminishing biodiversity. 这些变化也导致了生物栖息地的丧失和生物多样性的减少。（2008. 12） ② Don't let her diminish your achievements. 别让她贬低你的成就。
[00:53.72]exaggerate 熟义 v. 夸张，夸大 示例 ① The stakes have been vastly exaggerated. 风险被过分地夸大了。（2008. 6）② Her beauty has been greatly exaggerated. 她的美貌被过分夸大了。
[00:57.22]consult 熟义 v. 咨询，请教 示例 ① Through her book, 8 Myths of Making a Living, as well as workshops, seminars and personal coaching and consulting, she has helped thousands of dissatisfied workers reassess life and work. 通过她的著作《生活的八项迷思》以及一系列的专题讨论、研讨会和个人指导与咨询，她已经帮助了数以千计的不满员工重新对生活和工作进行了评估。（2007. 6）② Have you consulted your doctor about this? 你就此事咨询过你的医生吗？
[01:05.88]morality 熟义 n. 道德，道义；道德准则，道德规范 示例 ① There is considerable sentiment about the "corruption" of women's language—which of course is viewed as part of the loss of feminine ideals and morality—and this sentiment is crystallised by nationwide opinion polls that are regularly carried out by the media. 有很多关于妇女语言受到“玷污”的伤感——当然是被看作女性理想和道德丧失的一部分——而这种伤感是在媒体定期组织的全国性民意调查中确定的。（2007. 6）② Standards of morality seem to be deteriorating. 道德标准似乎一直在下降。 语料 Morality may consist solely in the courage of making a choice. 品德可能仅仅在于有勇气做出抉择。（布鲁斯）
[01:18.92]migrate 熟义 v. (鸟类、动物等)迁徙；移居，迁移 示例 ① The Pacific Whale Foundation on the west coast expressed concern that the scooters are frightening away an endangered species of whale that migrates to Hawaii for breeding. 位于西海岸的太平洋鲸鱼基金会表达了他们的担忧， 他们担心滑行艇吓跑了到夏威夷繁殖的一种濒危鲸鱼。（2008. 6）② Swallows migrate north in spring. 燕子在春天迁徙到北方。
[01:26.72]optimism 熟义 n. 乐观，乐观主义 示例 ① The Confederation of British Industry's May survey on the service sector points to an "outbreak of optimism" in the property world and a similar uptick in almost every consumer branch except travel. 英国工业联合会的五月份服务业调查指出，房产界出现了“乐观情绪爆发”，同样的情况几乎出现在除了旅游业外的每个消费部门。（The Economist）② You may now look forward with optimism. 你现在可以乐观地展望未来。
[01:35.55]seemingly 熟义 ad. 看似，貌似；据说，看来 示例 ① Tells fears that Mexican-Americans may be fated to follow in the footsteps of American blacks—that large parts of the community may become mired in a seemingly permanent state of poverty and underachievement. 大部分美国黑人都深陷无望的贫困，一生浑浑噩噩。 特勒斯担心，墨西哥裔美国人也可能命中注定会步美国黑人的后尘。（2008. 12） ② This is a seemingly stupid question. 这是一个看似愚蠢的问题。
[01:44.46]foremost 熟义 a. 最重要的，最前的‖ad. 最重要地 示例 ① While the West's foremost democracy stays paralysed, China is making decisions and forging ahead. 当西方最重要的民主处于瘫痪状态时，中国正在矢志不移地奋勇前进。（The Economist） ② She does a little teaching, but first and foremost she is a writer. 她从事一些教学工作，但首要的还是写作。
[01:51.20]notation 熟义 n. 记号，符号，谱号 示例 ① "That's my notation," he said. "When those black and white squares are going, that's what my hands do. I'm convinced it's all for a reason and it's my job to do it right." 他说：“那就是我的谱号。脑海中的黑白琴键如何移动，我的手就会怎样弹奏。我相信这其中一定有某种原因，而且我应该这样做。”（The Daily Mail）② The teacher asked his students to make a notation on the margin of the paper. 这位老师要求他的学生们在纸张空白边缘做个标记。
[02:00.43]revenge 熟义 n. 报仇，报复‖v. 报复，（向某人）报仇 示例 ① The rebels are now driven not by ideas of independence but by revenge or the vision of an Islamist state. 反叛分子现在不是被要求独立的思想所驱使，而是被仇恨或建立伊斯兰国家的幻想所驱使。（The Economist）② He vows to take revenge on his political enemies. 他发誓要报复他的政敌。
[02:06.88]trivial 熟义 a. 不重要的，琐碎的，微不足道的 示例 ① Individual examples can seem trivial, but the cumulative impact is significant. 个例看起来可能微不足道，但累积效应却意义重大。（The Economist）② I am sorry to bother you with such a trivial problem. 因为一个微不足道的问题打扰您， 我感到很抱歉。
[02:12.62]ascribe 熟义 v. 把…归因于，认为…是由于 示例 ① That those who believe in an afterlife ascribe mental acuity to the dead is hardly surprising. That those who do not are inclined to do so unless heavily prompted not to is curious indeed. 相信来世的人认为死去的人精神不灭，这一点都不奇怪，但那些不相信来世的人如果不是受到什么严重刺激而有这样的想法，实在是件奇怪事。（The Economist）② Tom ascribed his failure to bad luck. 汤姆认为自己的失败是由于运气不好。
[02:21.42]classical 熟义 a. 古典的，经典的 示例 ① He was the first classical music star of the television age; the only one feted with a ticker-tape parade; the first to sell a million copies of an album; above all he was the Texan who brushed the frost off the cold war with his huge hands, modest manner and electrifying renditions of great Russian composers. 他是电视时代的第一位古典音乐明星，唯一受到人们夹道欢迎的古典音乐明星，第一位单张专辑销量过百万的古典音乐明星。最重要的是，这名得克萨斯人用自己（弹奏钢琴）的大手、谦逊的态度和对俄国作曲家作品的激动人心的演绎扫去了冷战的冰霜。（The Economist）② He plays classical music, as well as rock. 他演奏古典音乐，同时也演奏摇滚乐。
[02:34.55]additive 熟义 n. 添加剂，添加物‖a. 添加的；【数】 加法的 示例 ① The assumption has been that genetic variants work in isolation, so their effects are additive: if you've got one variant that increases the risk of, say, heart disease 5 per cent and another that increases it 10 per cent, your overall risk is 15 per cent. 存在这么一种假设：基因变异是彼此独立发生的，因此其结果是可以累加的：如果你体内的一种变体能增加某种疾病，比如说心脏病5%的发病风险，而另一种变体能增加10%的发病风险，那么你总的发病风险为15%。（New Scientist）② Food additives may cause allergies. 食品添加剂可能引起过敏。
[02:46.07]versatile 熟义 a. 多才多艺的 示例 ① Quite by accident, eukaryotes' mindless efforts to deal with introns had made their genes more versatile and more evolvable. 纯属意外，真核细胞对付内含子的没头脑的努力使其自身基因更加多功能化，进化力更强。（New Scientist）② He's a very versatile performer. 他是个多才多艺的表演者。
[02:52.43]cynical 熟义 a. 愤世嫉俗的 示例 ① Some schools out for profit cynically increase tuitions and count on student loans and federal aid to foot the bill—knowing full well that the students won't make it. 一些学校为了追逐利润，可耻地提高了学费，甚至指望靠学生助学贷款和联邦政府补助支付它们的各项费用——虽然它们清楚地知道学生负担不起高昂的学费。（2011. 6）② He is cynical about everything. 他怀疑一切。
[03:00.17]underneath 熟义 prep. & ad. 在…底下；在…表象下‖n. 底面，底部 示例 ① What is clear is that underneath that smooth, calm surface, people are seething. 有一件事很清楚：在平静温和的外表之下，人们正怒火中烧。（The Economist） ② The coin rolled underneath the bed. 那枚硬币滚到了床底下。
[03:05.71]affirm 熟义 v. 肯定属实，断言，申明 示例 ① Some critics blame affirmative action—students admitted with lower test scores and grades from shaky high schools often struggle at elite schools. 一些批评者将矛头指向了平权行动——从教学质量差的高中录取的成绩差的学生通常在名校就读时会感到吃力。（2011. 6）② I can affirm that he will win the game. 我可以肯定他会赢得这场比赛。
[03:12.93]symphony 熟义 n. 交响乐，交响曲 示例 ① Sure, it's the first performance of the State Symphony Orchestra in our city, so suit and tie is a must. 当然，这是国家交响乐团在我们市的首次演出，所以西装和领带是必备的装束。② He is the principal cellist in the Beijing Symphony Orchestra. 他是北京交响乐团的首席大提琴手。
[03:19.01]contrary 熟义 a. 相反的‖n. 相反的事实、 情况等 示例 ① Contrary to popular belief, the more physicians taking care of you doesn't guarantee better care. 人们普遍认为，给你看病的医生越多你得到的治疗越好，但事实正好与此相反。（2009. 12）② Their criticism did not discourage him. On the contrary, he worked even harder. 他们的批评并没有使他气馁，相反，他比以前更加努力了。
[03:26.20]outer 熟义 a. 外边的；外围的 示例 ① We will be rubbing shoulders with aliens and colonising outer space. 我们将和外星生物来往，外太空将成为我们的聚居地。（2008. 6）② He lives in the outer suburbs of the city. 他住在城市的远郊。
[03:30.59]profile 熟义 n. 侧影；概述，简介；形象；轮廓‖v. 描…的轮廓 示例 ① In particular India has a handful of high-profile firms that are listed while being controlled by foreign firms, such as Suzuki, Nestlé, Unilever and Siemens. 特别是印度拥有一批知名度高的上市公司，它们由诸如铃木、雀巢、联合利华以及西门子等外国企业控制。（The Economist）② You should keep a low profile for the next few days. 未来几天里你要保持低调。
[03:38.79]primarily 熟义 ad. 主要地，根本地 示例 ① First, they have questioned whether the primary responsibility for digitally archiving the world's books should be allowed to fall to a commercial company. 首先，他们对能否将全球图书进行数字归档的主要责任交给一家商业公司的做法提出了质疑。（2011. 12）② This course is designed primarily for children. 这门课主要是为小孩子开设的。
[03:46.33]compete 熟义 v. 竞争；参加比赛 示例 ① Reynolds has argued that girls nowadays are using more assertive language strategies in order to be able to compete with boys in schools and out. 雷诺兹曾经指出，如今的女孩为了能够在学校内外和男孩竞争，都使用了更为自信的语言策略。（2007. 6）② We can't compete with the foreign companies on price. 我们在价格上无法与外国企业竞争。
[03:53.61]associate 熟义 vt. 联系，联想‖ a. 联合的，有关联的 示例 ① In many people's minds, energy conservation is still associated with self-denial. 很多人都认为，节约能源仍旧是一种克己的生活方式。（2007. 12）② I always associate the smell of baking with my grandma. 闻到烘烤食物的味道，我经常会想起我的祖母。
[03:59.49]perpetual 熟义 a. 不间断的，持续的；无尽无休的；终身的，永久的 示例 ① For those of us lucky enough to live that long, 2056 will be a world of almost perpetual youth, where obesity is a remote memory and robots become our companions. 对于我们中间那些有幸活到那时的人来说，在2056年人们几乎可以永葆青春，肥胖症成为遥远的记忆，机器人则成为我们的同伴。（2008. 6） ② How can I sleep with the perpetual noise of traffic? 交通噪音不断，让我怎么睡觉？
[04:07.97]reward 熟义 n. 奖励，报酬；悬赏金‖v. 奖励，奖赏 示例 ① Remove the pressure for primary care physicians to squeeze in more patients per hour, and reward them for optimally managing their diseases and practising evidence-based medicine. 除去初级护理医生每小时看更多病人的压力，并给予那些优化病患管理和基于病症用药的初级护理医师奖励。（2009. 12）② Our effort was finally rewarded. 我们的努力最终得到了回报。
[04:16.09]nevertheless 熟义 ad. 不过，然而，尽管如此 示例 ① Even if each element of immigration reform, taken in isolation, is agreed to be a good idea by a solid majority of Republican voters, Republican politicians must nevertheless avoid too-enthusiastically supporting this package of good ideas, lest they fail to project sufficient appreciation for the importance of keeping America American and putting Americans first. 即使移民改革的每一条方案，独立来看都被大多数共和党选举人认为是一个好主意，然而共和党政客也必须避免表现出过分热情地支持这一揽子好计划，否则他们将无法对保持美国由美国人治理以及将美国人放在首位的重要性表现出足够的重视。（The Economist）② There is little chance that we will win the game. Nevertheless, it is important that we try. 我们几乎没有可能赢得比赛。不过，重要的是我们应该努力争取。
[04:32.45]ideal 熟义 a. 完美的，理想的；不切实际的‖n. 理想；完美的人 示例 ① After critiquing the so-called thin ideal by writing essays and role-playing with their peers, participants are directed to come up with and execute small, nonviolent acts. 通过写文章和与同伴进行角色扮演的方式评论了所谓的苗条理想之后， 参与者被引导设计和执行小型的非暴力行为。（2009. 6）② This is an ideal place for a picnic. 这是理想的野餐地点。
[04:40.51]interpret 熟义 v. 诠释，说明；口译 示例 ① Instead we need a more dynamic interpretation, one that looks at the pros and cons of all the various ways land is used. 相反，我们需要一种更动态的理解方式，同时看到土地所有使用方式的正反两面。（2008. 12）② I didn't know whether I could interpret her smile as acceptance. 我不知道是否该把她的微笑看作接受。
[04:47.36]consumer 熟义 n. 消费者，顾客，用户 示例 ① There is no chance that will change anytime soon, even if the government creates a better social safety net and successfully encourages greater consumer spending. 即使政府建立了比较好的社会安全网络，成功地鼓励了民众扩大消费，中国人的这一审慎理财传统也不会马上改变。（2012. 12）② This supermarket provides a wider choice of goods for the consumer. 这个超市为消费者提供了更多种类的商品供选择。
[04:56.02]discipline 熟义 n. 纪律；行为准则；自制力 示例 ① There is considerable and justified concern that the United States is falling behind much of the rest of the developed world in these essential disciplines. 人们很担心，也有足够的理由担心，在这些基本学科领域，美国正落后于其他许多发达国家。（2010. 12）② It's a question of disciplining yourself to exercise every day. 这是个每天约束你自己锻炼的问题。
[05:04.07]illusion 熟义 n. 错误的观念，幻想；幻想的事物，错觉 示例 ① Some even think that real peace of mind is an illusion and cannot be attained. 一些人甚至认为内心的完全平静是一种错觉，是不可能达到的。（The Economist）② She's under the illusion that she will get married with the prince. 她幻想着她会嫁给王子。
